<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arco Etrusco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century BCE</span> · Also known as Etruscan Arch, Arch of Augustus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Arco Etrusco is a monumental gate in the Etruscan walls of Perugia in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, built in the 3rd century BCE. After Octavian took and burned the city in 40 BCE, it was restored and inscribed AUGUSTA PERUSIA, and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> loggia was later added on top. It is one of the best-preserved Etruscan city gates.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arco-etrusco.jpg" alt="Arco Etrusco" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francesco Gasparetti · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Perugia_Arco_Etrusco.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
